Package: tidybiotek
Title: Tidy Tools for Applied Biotechnology Bioinformatics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Jimmy", "Moses", , "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3342-2384"))
Description: Tidy, pipe-friendly tools for applied biotechnology
    bioinformatics. Covers DNA, RNA and protein sequence handling
    (translation, GC content, codon adaptation index, primer melting
    temperature, k-mer counts and codon optimisation), assay quantification
    (qPCR delta-delta Ct and Pfaffl ratios, four-parameter logistic
    dose-response curves with IC50 and EC50 estimates, and ELISA standard
    curves), bioprocess kinetics (Michaelis-Menten enzyme kinetics and
    Monod batch growth) and omics (moderated t-test differential
    expression and over-representation enrichment). Results are tibble
    subclasses built with 'vctrs' that keep their metadata through 'dplyr'
    verbs, and the package extends 'recipes', 'rsample', 'yardstick' and
    'parsnip' for biomarker and protein engineering workflows. Methods
    follow Sharp and Li (1987) <doi:10.1093/nar/15.3.1281>, SantaLucia
    (1998) <doi:10.1073/pnas.95.4.1460>, Livak and Schmittgen (2001)
    <doi:10.1006/meth.2001.1262>, Pfaffl (2001) <doi:10.1093/nar/29.9.e45>,
    Smyth (2004) <doi:10.2202/1544-6115.1027> and Truchon and Bayly (2007)
    <doi:10.1021/ci600426e>. Everything is written in base R and 'stats',
    with no Bioconductor or compiled dependencies.
